Ticket **#4471** was marked known as one parser bug. The merge put **two** causes in
the same ticket. Subject-line dedupe never asked which cause a report had.

## What is in #4471

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The split

- **`parser` — 379 reports.** The shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first
  tenants get the month and day flipped. This is the cause #4471 was opened for.
- **`hint` — 33 reports.** On booking-v3 the form prints `MM/DD/YYYY`. Day-first people
  type what the hint says; the form then reads the value the tenant's way. That is a
  different bug. It had no ticket of its own until we filed one.

<Callout kind="warn">
Two problems, two tickets. #4471 was never only one bug.
</Callout>

## Filed

- [#1 parser — 379 reports](https://github.com/janozis/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) —
  closed **completed** after `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`
- [#2 hint — 33 reports](https://github.com/janozis/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) —
  closed **not planned**; booking-v3 form retired

## Desk update · #4471 closed 05 Oct

- **parser** — fixed
- **hint** — won't fix

